{"name":"Pantomime","hex":"#adafba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pantomime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Classical comic actor, especially one who works mainly through gesture and mime. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The drama in ancient Greece and Rome featuring such performers; or (later) any of various kinds of performance modelled on such work."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (a gesture) without speaking.","To entertain others by silent gestures or actions. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pantomime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pantomime","blocks":[{"text":"Pantomime is a type of musical comedy stage production designed for family entertainment, generally combining broad and topical humour and cross-dressing actors with a story based on a well-known fairy tale, fable or folk tale. Pantomime is a participatory form of theatre developed in England in the 18th century in which the audience is encouraged and expected to sing along with certain parts of the music and to shout out phrases to the performers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Warne_Pantomine_1890.jpg/330px-Warne_Pantomine_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantomime","wikidata":"Q13409536"},{"title":"Pantomime (The Pillows EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Pantomime (パントマイム) is an EP / mini-album released by The Pillows on May 21, 1990. It marked the band's debut commercial release and has since, like its follow-up 90's My Life, gone out of print. Despite this, it can often be found on Japanese auction websites ranging from ¥4,000 – ¥5,000 JPY."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/The_pillows_-_pantomime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantomime_(The_Pillows_EP)","wikidata":"Q11329701"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Ancient_Macedonian_antefix_2nd_century_A.D.jpg/500px-Ancient_Macedonian_antefix_2nd_century_A.D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Ancient_Macedonian_antefix_2nd_century_A.D.jpg/500px-Ancient_Macedonian_antefix_2nd_century_A.D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"2nd-century Macedonian theatrical sculpture, thought to represent a pantomime's mask","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAncient_Macedonian_antefix_2nd_century_A.D.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Richarlequin.jpg/500px-Richarlequin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Richarlequin.jpg/500px-Richarlequin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Rich as Harlequin, c. 1720","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARicharlequin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Pantomime_1803.jpg/500px-Pantomime_1803.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Pantomime_1803.jpg/500px-Pantomime_1803.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Playbill of an English circus and pantomime performance, 1803","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APantomime_1803.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Harvard_Theatre_Collection_-_Grimaldi_%282%29_MS_Thr_847.jpg/500px-Harvard_Theatre_Collection_-_Grimaldi_%282%29_MS_Thr_847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Harvard_Theatre_Co